%I A025270 #17 Nov 05 2026 04:01:00
%S A025270 1,2,1,1,6,17,60,201,688,2370,8218,28703,100846,356370,1265918,
%T A025270 4518571,16200070,58317298,210718174,764015412,2778955460,10137598506,
%U A025270 37082361204,135985402371,499840932062,1841260760276,6796395432602,25134116857096
%N A025270 a(n) = a(1)*a(n-1) + a(2)*a(n-2) + ...+ a(n-1)*a(1) for n >= 5, with initial values 1,2,1,1.
%F A025270 Conjecture: n*a(n) +2*(-2*n+3)*a(n-1) +4*(-n+3)*a(n-2) +6*(2*n-9)*a(n-3) +20*(n-6)*a(n-4)=0. - _R. J. Mathar_, Nov 21 2014
%F A025270 G.f.: 1/2 - sqrt(20*x^4+12*x^3-4*x^2-4*x+1)/2. - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Jan 25 2015
%F A025270 The conjectured recurrence follows from the given generating function. Let A(x) = (1-sqrt(Q(x)))/2, where Q(x)=1-4*x-4*x^2+12*x^3+20*x^4. From (1-2*A(x))^2=Q(x), differentiating and multiplying by 1-2*A(x) gives 4*Q(x)*A'(x)-2*Q'(x)*A(x)+Q'(x) = 0. Equating coefficients of x^(n-1), for n >= 5, gives the conjectured recurrence. - _Eiver Rodríguez_, Nov 04 2026
%t A025270 nmax = 30; aa = ConstantArray[0,nmax]; aa[[1]] = 1; aa[[2]] = 2; aa[[3]] = 1; aa[[4]] = 1; Do[aa[[n]] = Sum[aa[[k]]*aa[[n-k]],{k,1,n-1}],{n,5,nmax}]; aa (* _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Jan 25 2015 *)
%Y A025270 Cf. A025268.
%K A025270 nonn,changed
%O A025270 1,2
%A A025270 _Clark Kimberling_
